{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_19-20-29-omnipaxos-real-run/draft && cat > update.json <<'JSON'\n{\n  \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Second turn: ran selected, named tests from the fork's own actor test file plus a new in-process 3-node core battery (draft/tmp/ws/omnipaxos/tests/probe1.rs, probe2.rs, probe3.rs) as construction feedback. Basic agreement, batching content correctness, StopSign reconfiguration, follower crash/recover catch-up, leader-change agreement, sequence-gap resync after a dropped AcceptDecide, and duplicate delivery all hold locally. Two probes initially failed on my own expectations rather than on the target (18 forwarded entries vs 9 unique values; and reading a decided suffix whose prefix is compacted yields a leading compaction marker, so a per-index equality check is invalid). That second observation is source-settled into a knowledge fact, because it contradicts the actor layer's per-index cursor assumption. Question @quorum_lengths is answered from source: the accept-phase support count is over log lengths. Next action is a retained multi-case experiment in the omnipaxos package covering the recovery/compaction interactions that my local driver cannot settle.\\\",\n  \\\"sources\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"read_path\\\",\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"omnipaxos/src/storage/internal_storage.rs\\\",\n      \\\"start_line\\\": 76,\n      \\\"end_line\\\": 157,\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"code_observation\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"actor_subscribers\\\",\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"omnipaxos_runtime/src/actor.rs\\\",\n      \\\"start_line\\\": 279,\n      \\\"end_line\\\": 333,\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"code_observation\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"actor_handle_read\\\",\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"omnipaxos_runtime/src/handle.rs\\\",\n      \\\"start_line\\\": 242,\n      \\\"end_line\\\": 254,\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"interface_statement\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"knowledge\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"ref\\\": \\\"@decided_suffix_compaction_marker\\\",\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"behavior\\\",\n      \\\"statement\\\": \\\"\"'`InternalStorage::read_decided_suffix(from_idx)` delegates to `read(from_idx..decided_idx)`, and `read` returns a single leading compaction marker (`LogEntry::Trimmed(compacted_idx)` or `LogEntry::Snapshotted(..)`) whenever the upper end of the requested range lies inside the compacted prefix. Consequently, when `from_idx < compacted_idx`, the returned vector'\"'s element at position k is NOT the log entry at index from_idx + k: position 0 is the marker for the whole compacted prefix and the following elements correspond to indices compacted_idx, compacted_idx+1, ....\\\",\n      \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"Captured snapshot; holds for any range whose exclusive end \"'`to_idx` satisfies `to_idx - 1 < compacted_idx` (the `get_entry_type(to_idx - 1, ...) == Compacted` early return), i.e. whenever the requested decided suffix starts inside or entirely below the compacted prefix; the public wrappers (`OmniPaxos::read_decided_suffix`, `OmniPaxosHandle::read_decided_suffix`) do not re-align or clamp `from_idx`.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\"read_path\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@actor_subscriber_cursor\",\n      \"kind\": \"behavior\",\n      \"statement\": \"Both decided-log fan-out paths in the actor advance the per-subscriber cursor by exactly one per element returned by `read_decided_suffix` (`push_to_sub`: `sub.next_idx += 1` per successful `try_send`; `push_to_all_subs`: `start = sub.next_idx.saturating_sub(min_next)` then one increment per element sent). They therefore treat a returned element as being at index `next_idx + i`, which is only true while the subscriber'\"'s start index is at or above the node's compacted index.\\\",\n      \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"Captured snapshot; \"'`Command::SubscribeDecided { from }` with `from < get_compacted_idx()` on that node, i.e. subscribing (or re-subscribing) to a decided log whose prefix has already been trimmed or snapshotted.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\"actor_subscribers\", \"read_path\", \"actor_handle_read\"],\n      \"knowledge\": [\n        {\n          \"entry_id\": \"@decided_suffix_compaction_marker\",\n          \"revision\": 1,\n          \"assertion\": \"read_decided_suffix(from_idx < compacted_idx) returns a leading compaction marker instead of an entry at from_idx\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"interpretations\": [\n    {\n      \"investigation_id\": \"5d087c25407e4157b6b06176a649ef5c-question-2\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\"quorum\", \"leader_accepted\", \"batching\"],\n      \"conclusion\": \"holds\",\n      \"defect_claim\": null,\n      \"rationale\": \"Source-only reading settles the premise the question asked about: `InternalStorage` maintains `accepted_idx` as a log LENGTH (`AppendEntries`/`AppendSync` semantics: `state_cache.accepted_idx = sync.sync_idx + sync.suffix.len()`, increment by one per appended entry and by one for a StopSign), `LeaderState.accepted_indexes` is seeded with 0 for every pid and written with that same length (`set_accepted_idx`) or with a follower-reported length (`handle_accepted` -> `set_accepted_idx(from, accepted.accepted_idx)`), `is_chosen(idx)` counts entries with `accepted_indexes[k] >= idx`, and the leader passes the reported length (`accepted.accepted_idx`) as well as its own length. `get_min_all_accepted_idx` (used by `trim(None)`) takes the minimum of the same lengths. So the decide step, the trim step and the reported values agree on length semantics; no off-by-one between them is visible in the captured code.\",\n      \"counterevidence\": [\n        \"The name `accepted_idx` reads like an entry index, and `read_decided_suffix`/`read` use indices; any future consumer that mixes the two conventions would be off by one, but no such consumer is present in the captured code paths I read.\"\n      ],\n      \"limitations\": [\n        \"This is a source-only account; it establishes the units used by the captured code, not that every message producer/consumer pair is consistent at runtime, which the experiment in this update does not yet cover.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\nJSON\npython3 -c \"import json;json.load(open('\"'update.json'));print('ok')\\\"\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_19-20-29-omnipaxos-real-run --submission update.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
